' lint-ok: a building block is no business process, so it owns no BPxx call sites (ADR-069)
@startbpmn BB22_WorkLoop
lang en

output L1 "BB22_WorkLoop.bpmn"

' The frame thirteen processes are built on, drawn once so no act block redraws it. It asks the
' system for nothing of its own, which is why it has no system pool: what it carries is the
' skeleton - the trigger, the surface the act is performed on, the one question, and one path per
' act, each ending on what its gesture did. A member varies the vocabulary and the number of
' branches, never the shape.
'
' THE LOOP IS NOT HERE ANY MORE. That the surface stays in front of the user and the next act is
' available is a user-interface fact, drawn once in UIP01 as a loop marker on the surface's box,
' not as a return edge per act in every process: SA 2026-10-17, DRW-09.

pool "User" {
  start "A <entity> needs attention"
  :Open the <view>;
  note "Opening it is OpenView: one request, one answer, and the question decides on that answer."
  :Work a <entity>;
  rule BR-118
  if "What needs doing?" then "an act"
    :Perform one act;
    note "One branch per act, each of them a block: EditContent, EditState, ArchiveLeafItem, DeleteCascadedItem, UnarchiveItem, a hand-over to a sub-process, a seam. An act never asks the user to re-read the view afterwards."
    end "<What the gesture did>"
  elseif "What needs doing?" then "another act"
    :Perform another one;
    end "<What that gesture did>"
  endif
}

@endbpmn
